WEBVTT

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.310
I don't have a brother!

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:14.740
I don't have any family!

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.010
I...

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.010
...always...

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.040
...wanted to be in Riko-chan's place.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.520
That's why...

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.790
That's why I...

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.830
Just when and where did things go wrong between us...

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.160
These feelings that I couldn't even tell my friends about

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:56.490
are still locked up inside me even now

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.580
If I eat the magical fruit inside my heart

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:06.550
they might actually be able to come out

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.160
I kept on waiting in the classroom

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.160
making excuses that it's just a coincidence

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.750
That smile is probably meant for someone

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:28.210
If dreams can make my wishes come true

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.160
I want to give you this present

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:38.330
I will transform your rainbow

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:43.290
into a bridge of happiness, just wave to me

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.570
It's all right, it's all right

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.920
I simply want to watch over you...

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.980
<i>The Secret of Gift</i>

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.260
And lastly, some seasoning...

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.140
An appropriate amount?

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.350
How much would that be?

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.950
I'm not sure, but this will probably do.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.930
Riko!

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.760
I made you some porridge!

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.610
Hey, Riko?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.060
Riko.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.110
What are you doing?

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.070
Hey.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.150
What's wrong?

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.390
I can't remember...

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.910
Not a thing...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.290
This is me in this picture, right?

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:08.690
I seem so happy...

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:13.080
I'm sure this is a place where I was happy.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.100
But there is nothing!

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.380
There is nothing left!

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.210
Even though it's supposed to be so important...

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.390
I have nothing left anymore!

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.760
It's okay.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.940
I'll bring everything back for you.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:30.120
There's no need to worry.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.300
I'm sorry...

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.480
I'm sorry!

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.110
Sorry!

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.270
Everything will be fine.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.880
<i>Didn't Gift...</i>

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.780
<i>Didn't Gift exist to bring happiness to the people!?</i>

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.960
That expression.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:56.550
Did a billion of your brain cells die off recently?

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.400
Yeah.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.160
An interesting response.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:05.070
Incidentally, it seems Fukamine-san is absent today.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.740
She didn't feel well.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.020
She's sleeping at home.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.310
I heard Konosaka-san was absent as well.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:15.150
You likely want to tell me it's just a coincidence...

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.270
...but unfortunately for you, I don't believe that.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.490
Can you help me out with this?

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.570
I'll lend you an ear.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.170
I see.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.830
That was quite an interesting story.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.100
I treated you to a drink and that's all I get for it?

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.560
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.690
But up until now, deflected Gifts have always been...

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.130
It wasn't deflected.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:47.040
Fukamine-san accepted Konosaka-san's Gift.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.930
In other words, the Gift was correctly used.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:58.860
This place...

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.570
...keeps reappearing in my dreams.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.870
Memories between Haruhiko-kun and Riko-chan...

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.240
Very sad memories...

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.340
Riko!

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.840
Farewell...

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:24.840
Riko-chan...

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.370
Sorry...

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.070
I'm sorry...

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:35.680
I wasn't the only one suffering, was I?

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:45.630
So what you are trying to do...

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.820
...is to fight against Gift itself.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:49.700
Yeah...

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:52.950
Gift is as precious as your own life.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.450
You are the one who kept saying that.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.480
Right now, I'm prepared to do anything it takes.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.490
In that case, you have no need for my advice.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.130
What's wrong?

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.270
I thought you were prepared for this?

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.220
Is erasing it really the only way?

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.160
What should I do?

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.660
Knowing your enemy is the path to victory.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.560
That is, knowing what Gift really is.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.740
Everything in this world has a causal relation to something else.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:27.570
Remove the cause, and its consequence will disappear as well.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.890
What caused Gift to come into existence?

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.180
That's what you have to find out.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.690
Why was Gift created?

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.610
That's a difficult question.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:49.010
You've been researching Gift for a long time, haven't you?

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.930
Please tell me anything you know.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.630
In essence, we still don't know a thing.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:54.890
Let me see...

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:59.270
All we know is that Gift was suddenly brought into existence at a certain point in time.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.170
When?

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:01.350
Let's see...

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.610
Seventeen years ago.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.300
Seventeen?

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:08.360
Did it happen the year I was born?

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:09.900
I guess so.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.960
But in this period the eternal rainbow did not exist yet.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:13.960
Naturally.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.810
Never mind.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:16.880
What else?

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:19.330
I have some more specific data here...

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.270
Got it!

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.980
Gift was first confirmed...

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.950
...on April 15th of that year.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.020
What's wrong?

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.350
That's my birthday!

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.340
I see.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.140
A coincidence?

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:37.350
Gift came into being on your birthday?

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.650
An interesting correspondence.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.100
It might as well be just a coincidence.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:45.820
Don't you think those two events might be causally related?

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:46.900
No way!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.420
I'd like to believe that as well.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:52.440
I can't condone you being worshipped like some sort of god.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.710
God?

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.500
Don't be ridiculous.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.820
Is there something strange about them?

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:03.370
Gift has fulfilled a large number of wishes in this town.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.080
If you have indeed brought Gift into existence...

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.050
...that would make you a being akin to a god to these people.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.850
Though I really don't wish to use unscientific words like "god."

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:15.680
I am no god.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:21.390
I am planning to erase the Gift that is so important to everyone, after all.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.400
Calling me a demon would suit me better.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:26.680
Enough of that.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.700
Let's leave our unscientific conversation for what it is.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:33.780
Can you think of anything else that happened on your birthday?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.860
Something else, huh...

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:37.910
Anything at all.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.030
No ideas?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.770
Let me think...

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.540
That's right, that day is my mother's...

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:45.690
What?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.440
It's the day my mother passed away.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.950
Interesting.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.690
Are you trying to say my mother is responsible for it?

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.470
We can't disregard the possibility.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.960
It's not possible.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.270
My mother <i>used </i> a Gift.

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.220
My father often told me.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:02.640
My life was given to me by my mother.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:05.860
You were a premature baby.

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:09.350
You were able to grow up healthily thanks to your mother.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:10.990
Thanks to Mom?

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:11.880
That's right.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.740
Your mother gave you life itself.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.240
Thanks to her Gift, right?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.040
Oh, yeah...

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.200
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:26.750
Your mother gave you the most precious thing before she died.

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:30.250
My life is Mom's Gift.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.490
Yeah.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:33.840
That's why you should cherish your life.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.630
Yeah!

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:36.450
That's why...

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.310
...I've treasured Gift more than anyone else.

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:40.290
And yet...

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.530
How odd.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:48.020
That would mean your mother used Gift on the very day it was born.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.960
Meaning my mother was the first user of Gift?

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.950
No, that doesn't quite follow either.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.820
Your mother passed away on that same day, didn't she?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.130
Can you really use Gift at a time like that?

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:02.230
Right, that's strange indeed.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.880
Then the Gift Mom used was...

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.500
Damn, I have no clue!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.250
About the day your mother died?

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.000
Yes, please tell me about it.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.040
I need to make sure of something.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:20.140
What would that be?

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:23.290
Mom died on the day I was born.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:24.680
That is correct, right?

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:28.640
Well, Dad?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:34.580
You weren't born on April 15th.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.990
You were in fact born on April 1st.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:40.770
You were a premature baby.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:44.800
If this caused your development to fall behind schedule, you might have gotten in trouble at school.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:46.240
Since we were worried about that...

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.820
...we decided to put off your birthday so you could enter school a year later.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:54.230
My real birthday is April 1st?

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.370
Sorry for keeping it from you.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.280
Then when did Mom pass away?

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.590
That was indeed the 15th.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.070
I see...

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:04.850
Wait a sec.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.790
That means, in the two weeks before her death...

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:10.400
...she was able to see me and touch me?

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.430
Yeah.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:14.430
She was able to hold you in her arms on the same day she died.

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:18.360
Just in time for your release from the incubator.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:21.250
She... held me in her arms?

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.420
She was very delighted.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:24.440
I see...

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.580
So that's how it was...

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:29.570
Two weeks is a short time.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.090
But... she did get to see me!

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.660
I had physical contact with my mother!

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.090
I wish you'd told me sooner.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:48.980
I always thought my mother passed away without ever seeing my face.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:50.140
Sorry.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:51.520
That wasn't very considerate of me.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.230
That's just like you.

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:01.440
<i>The day Gift was created.</i>

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.000
<i>On that same day, Mom died.</i>

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.020
<i>Please tell me.</i>

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:10.090
<i>Are your death and Gift related?</i>

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.870
Did the continuous rain cause fungi to develop inside your head?

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:25.470
What is it?

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.960
Why don't you try to look alive for once?

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.390
Adolescence comes with many troubles.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:32.450
What do you want?

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:34.350
You have guests in the hallway.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:39.340
Kirinon hasn't come to school for a while.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.610
She won't meet me even if I ask her...

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:46.290
We thought you might know something about it...

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:50.240
Riko-san seems to have been absent for a while now as well.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.130
Well... a lot of things have happened.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.330
I don't know how to say this, but...

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.940
...I can't help but feel something unpleasant has happened.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.530
Oh boy.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.840
Riko and Kirino are making their friends worry so much...

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:06.700
Don't worry!

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:08.290
I'll do something about it.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:09.100
Really?

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:12.210
They'll be back soon.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:13.810
I promise.

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:19.700
You're going home early.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:20.660
Yeah.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.160
No use moping around like this.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.820
Time to take action.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:27.780
You've finally become yourself again.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:29.030
See ya.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.540
You can't stop me.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.930
You are dismissed.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.720
I'm going to see Mom.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.200
Maybe...

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.240
...Mom created Gift.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:56.230
If that is the case, Gift would be my life itself.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.100
But...

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:00.730
...despite that I am still prepared to erase Gift.

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:03.350
In order to protect the person I love.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.860
Onii-chan...

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:22.250
Long time no see, Mom.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.410
I have something important to ask you.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.680
I am sure you know.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.180
<i>Amami family grave</i>

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.180
What Gift really is.

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.560
Gift was born on the day you died.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.690
There's a connection, isn't there?

00:14:42.050 --> 00:14:43.690
Please tell me!

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.070
I want to save Riko!

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.880
My important...

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.490
...most important person!

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:52.560
I'll do anything to protect her!

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.450
I beg of you, Mom!

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:08.980
<i>A hospital?</i>

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:10.740
<i>What am I doing here?</i>

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.010
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.480
Look, Haru!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:21.090
The cutest kid in this room is our son!

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.440
<i>No way...</i>

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.280
<i>Is that... Dad?</i>

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.580
<i>That means the person next to him is...</i>

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.140
What are you talking about?

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:33.380
They all have wrinkled faces like that of little monkeys.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:34.750
<i>No doubt about it.</i>

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:35.780
<i>It's Mom!</i>

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:40.400
No, his cuteness is plain as day!

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:41.270
See?

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.500
That is someone else's child!

00:15:43.930 --> 00:15:45.040
R-Really!?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.420
Babies really look alike, don't they!?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.560
Oh, you!

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:57.010
<i>Is this the day I was born?</i>

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.950
<i>That's right... Mom was still alive at this point.</i>

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.020
<i>She was still alive!</i>

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.810
I'm sorry.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:07.070
<i>April 5th</i>

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.540
I'm having trouble producing breast milk...

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:06.750
It's okay.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.280
There are times when nothing comes out.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:09.420
But...

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.970
I haven't been able to since yesterday...

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.160
Don't worry.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.240
Have a good meal and a good night's sleep.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.620
A mother shouldn't be looking that depressed!

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:19.830
Okay.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:24.880
It must be hard for Amami-san.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:26.790
Her baby was born prematurely...

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:29.960
Her own condition isn't very good either.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:31.870
There seem to be problems with her heart.

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:32.990
That can't be...

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:36.150
If worse comes to worst, what will happen to the baby?

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:42.310
<i>April 9th</i>

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.680
He looks like a glass sculpture...

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.020
Like he would break if I merely touched him.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.690
It's okay.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.070
You can touch him.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:48.940
Haruhiko...

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:54.570
What's wrong?

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:56.940
I was just...

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:59.230
...suddenly moved to tears.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:00.850
Maternity blues?

00:17:00.850 --> 00:17:03.580
Nothing like that!

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:05.790
I was moved.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.950
It's such a small life...

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.460
...yet he is properly growing.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.590
Yeah...

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:13.420
I wish we had a little more time together...

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.220
Haru...

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.800
I want to live.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:18.180
I feel that way from the bottom of my heart.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.020
Even for one more minute...

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:21.140
For one more second...

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:23.060
I want to keep living.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:28.780
I never imagined I'd get so scared to die...

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:35.740
<i>April 12th</i>

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.590
So here's where you were.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.110
I was looking for you.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.340
Sorry.

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:38.980
There was a rainbow out.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:41.580
You sure love rainbows, don't you?

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:44.480
Let's go back to your room.

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.020
What about your work?

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.800
It's fine today!

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.670
I have to take days off every once in a while.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.390
Liar.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:56.340
A workaholic like you can't afford that.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:59.000
I'm aware...

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.630
...that I don't have much time left.

00:18:01.630 --> 00:18:03.220
T-That's not true!

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:10.770
I've been thinking about what to leave behind for Haruhiko.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.090
Leave behind?

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.960
Something like a memento.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.740
What do you think would be appropriate?

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.170
H-How would I know!?

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:20.740
Stop being silly and get back to your room!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:22.470
Your condition will worsen again.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:28.750
<i>April 13th</i>

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.840
I'm a little worried.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:37.800
Will you and your father really be all right after I'm gone?

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:40.810
Your father is a good person...

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.810
...but he is so unexperienced...

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:46.500
I really wish I could be there for you...

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.360
Haru-san!?

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.360
Call the doctor!

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:03.080
<i>April 15th</i>

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:06.080
Are you okay?

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.280
Yes.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:08.520
I'm sorry...

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.700
Where is Haruhiko?

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:11.070
He is sleeping.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:12.230
By the way.

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:15.150
We're allowed to take him out of the incubator now.

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:16.200
Really?

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:20.320
No, you have to rest now.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.720
Did the rain stop?

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:25.020
Yeah.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:26.100
Just now.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:30.810
Beautiful...

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:36.340
I want to show this to Haruhiko.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:39.320
You can show him as much as you want afterwards.

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.570
There won't be an afterwards...

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.560
I'll buy you something to drink.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:48.080
Dear...

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.340
I finally thought of something.

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:54.120
Something to leave behind for him.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:56.090
Are you still going on about that?

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.660
For Haruhiko to grow strong...

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.670
For his future...

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:04.930
I want to give him something very precious.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:08.310
My first and final gift to him.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:10.620
Hey...

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:12.520
I'm going to see Haruhiko.

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.490
Was that a dream...?

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:23.380
No, it wasn't.

00:20:23.380 --> 00:20:24.580
I saw it!

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:26.360
I saw it with my own eyes!

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:31.000
I finally understand.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.670
How Gift was born.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.000
What Mom gave me was not my life.

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:39.100
It was something more important than that.

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:41.290
Thank you.

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:45.430
The fact that I was able to make it to this point is thanks to you.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.260
But...

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.680
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.100
I'm going to erase Gift.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:53.890
I want to protect Riko...

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.030
I want to protect the person most dear to me.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.710
To do that, I will erase Gift.

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.650
I have to erase it!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:07.620
Thank you...

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:09.450
...Mom.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:12.290
<i>Gift.</i>

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:17.840
<i>The mysterious power to make a miracle happen once in a lifetime.</i>

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:21.880
<i>Right now, I will use that power.</i>

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.930
<i>In order to erase Gift itself.</i>

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:33.230
<i>I will protect the person I love with my own hands.</i>

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:39.310
<i>I will bring back the smile to her face with my own hands.</i>

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:51.080
Gift!

00:22:12.170 --> 00:22:16.350
In a corner of the classroom

00:22:17.240 --> 00:22:22.940
I hummed my favourite song

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:28.870
Why did those melancholic feelings

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:33.100
well up within me today

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:40.140
When I return, will this town

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:43.930
gently welcome me back?

00:22:43.930 --> 00:22:48.120
Hey, I want to meet you

00:22:49.680 --> 00:22:55.240
In times you feel down, I wish you would tell me

00:22:55.240 --> 00:23:00.160
before you can no longer turn back

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:04.110
Building a heartfelt rainbow together

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:06.920
Say that I'm not alone

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:12.990
So that my prayers may be heard

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:33.080
The rainbow has disappeared from this town.

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:36.220
But I finally understand.

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:40.590
As long as people think about each other, a rainbow will always appear.

00:23:41.170 --> 00:23:42.230
No matter how often.

00:23:43.790 --> 00:23:46.300
Let's chase the rainbow to wherever it leads.

00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:48.150
Just the two of us.

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:52.240
Next time, "The Eternal Rainbow."

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:59.960
<i>The Eternal Rainbow</i>

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:54.270
Gift.

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:57.750
Giving thanks to everyone.
